From 9da61378bc4784ec5f4837eec781ad654c8ee9c6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jason Zaugg <jzaugg@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 07:54:33 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] Register the names of a classOf literal's type as used names

The typer folds `classOf[Foo]` into a `Literal` whose constant holds the
type, so `ExtractUsedNames` saw no tree naming `Foo`. `Dependency` already
records the class of such a literal, but with no used name the name-hash
filter skips the client when `Foo` changes in that class, and the
added-class rules (rz#34, rz#47) never reach it when a new class makes
`Foo` resolve elsewhere or become ambiguous.

`ExtractUsedNames` now traverses the type of a `classOf` constant as it
does an inferred type.

`classof-used-name` (N1 in rz#42) now passes. The new
`classof-added-java-class-ambiguous` is the Java-space conformance shape:
a Java class added behind a wildcard import makes `Foo` ambiguous.
